ate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/algotree/</guid><description>An immutable-by-default tree library for Python with composable transformations, pipe-based pipelines, and pattern-matching selectors.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/algotree/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Data-Structures</media:title></media:content><category>Python</category><category>data-structures</category><category>trees</category><category>functional-programming</category><category>immutability</category><category>pattern-matching</category></item><item><title>Packed Containers: Zero-Waste Bit-Level Storage in C++</title><link>https://queelius.github.io/post/2018-10-packed-containers/</link><pubDate>Mon, 15 Oct 2018 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><dc:creator>Alex Towell</dc:creator><guid isPermaLink="true">https://queelius.github.io/post/2018-10-packed-containers/</guid><description>What if containers wasted zero bits? A C++ library for packing arbitrary value types at the bit level using pluggable codecs.</description><media:content url="https://queelius.github.io/post/2018-10-packed-containers/card.jpg" medium="image"><media:title type="plain">Data-Structures</media:title></media:content><category>C++</category><category>data-structures</category><category>information-theory</category><category>generic-programming</category></item></channel></rss>